WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.941
Why connect education, businesses, and administration in
one platform?

00:00:03.941 --> 00:00:08.319
I am PARIS, your AI presenter for Elevate for Humanity.

00:00:08.319 --> 00:00:11.822
A learner's journey involves more than a course.

00:00:11.822 --> 00:00:17.952
There may be an inquiry, an application, a funding
review, training, assessments, employer coordination,

00:00:17.952 --> 00:00:19.266
and completion records.

00:00:19.266 --> 00:00:25.396
Elevate presents its platform as a way to coordinate
those stages through role based

00:00:25.396 --> 00:00:25.833
workspaces.

00:00:25.833 --> 00:00:31.963
Imagine a provider using a consistent checklist so
participants know what happens next and

00:00:31.963 --> 00:00:34.590
staff can find the right record.

00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:38.969
The goal is less repeated explanation and better follow
through.

00:00:38.969 --> 00:00:43.785
Actual time savings depend on the workflow,
configuration, training, and adoption.

00:00:43.785 --> 00:00:49.477
Do not assume a demonstration proves every integration
is active for your organization.

00:00:49.477 --> 00:00:53.418
Ask to test the exact steps your team needs.

00:00:53.418 --> 00:00:58.235
Include accessibility, permissions, mobile access, and
human support in that review.

00:00:58.235 --> 00:01:04.364
For learners balancing family and work, clearer
instructions and online materials can help with

00:01:04.364 --> 00:01:08.743
planning, but hands on requirements and travel may still
apply.

00:01:08.743 --> 00:01:11.808
Funding is reviewed by program and participant.

00:01:11.808 --> 00:01:17.062
Apprenticeships are self pay unless the exact program
documents another approved source.

00:01:17.062 --> 00:01:22.316
Explore programs, employers, and the platform at Elevate
for Humanity dot org.

00:01:22.316 --> 00:01:28.446
Share this episode with a school, employer, or community
organization that wants a more

00:01:28.446 --> 00:01:29.760
connected participant journey.

